{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
{% set title = "Community site sections" %}
{% set slug = "patterns-community" %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Community site sections</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Sections from a volunteer group's site, modelled on
  <a href="https://lzr.life" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lzr.life</a>:
  a catalog to browse, a how-to, and events. These lean on the content and form
  components more than the studio sections do. The rules behind them are on
  <a href="./composition.html">Composition</a>.
</p>

<section id="hero">
  <h2>Welcome with a quote</h2>
  <p>
    The whole site is re-themed from one input on the root element. Here it is
    on the section instead, so you can see it next to the default theme.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="retheme prose" style="--primary: #a33b2b; --neutral: #6b6150; max-width: 40rem">
  <h1>Little Zine Revolution</h1>
  <p>We curate and distribute anti-colonial zines. Little actions have ripple effects.</p>
  <blockquote>
    You have to act as if it were possible to radically transform the world. And
    you have to do it all the time.
    <footer class="text-secondary"><small>Angela Davis</small></footer>
  </blockquote>
  <a href="#" class="btn">Explore the zine catalog</a>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-hero", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Boundary:</strong> <code>--primary</code> sets the button and the quote's rule. <code>--neutral</code> sets what text and surfaces are tinted with, so the page reads warm and muted while the brand colour stays saturated.</li>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> the attribution sits inside the <code>blockquote</code> so the quote's rule runs the full height of both.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="how-to-help">
  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <p>
    Three equal steps, each linking deeper into a guide. Numbering is part of the
    heading, so it needs no counter styles.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Print! Fold! Distribute!</h2>
  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)">
    <div class="card-border">
      <h3>1. Printing</h3>
      <p class="text-secondary">Pick a zine from the catalog and print it at home or at a library.</p>
      <a href="#" class="link">Printing tips</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card-border">
      <h3>2. Folding</h3>
      <p class="text-secondary">Join a folding event, or follow the guide on your own.</p>
      <a href="#" class="link">Folding instructions</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card-border">
      <h3>3. Distribution</h3>
      <p class="text-secondary">Leave copies in a little free library near you.</p>
      <a href="#" class="link">Distribution guide</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-steps", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Actions:</strong> each card holds a real link rather than being one, because the card has a sentence worth reading on its own. Compare the <a href="./patterns-studio.html#case-studies">case study cards</a>, where the card is the link.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="catalog">
  <h2>Catalog with filters</h2>
  <p>
    A search field, a segmented control for the one exclusive choice, checkboxes
    for the ones that combine, and a grid of results.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<form class="card-border">
  <label class="label">
    <p>Search</p>
    <input class="input" type="search" placeholder="Title or topic" />
  </label>
  <div class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center">
    <div class="segmented" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Fold">
      <label class="segmented-item"><input type="radio" name="fold" checked /> Any fold</label>
      <label class="segmented-item"><input type="radio" name="fold" /> Quarters</label>
      <label class="segmented-item"><input type="radio" name="fold" /> Trifold</label>
    </div>
    <label class="label" style="margin: 0">
      <input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" /> Colour
    </label>
    <label class="label" style="margin: 0">
      <input type="checkbox" class="checkbox" checked /> Double sided
    </label>
  </div>
</form>

<p class="text-secondary" style="margin: var(--padding) 0"><small>3 of 62 zines</small></p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(9rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)">
  <a href="#" class="semantic card">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>For the Love of Bread</strong>
    <p><span class="badge">Quarters</span></p>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic card">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Anarchist Compass</strong>
    <p><span class="badge">Trifold</span></p>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic card">
    <div style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; background: var(--surface-strong); border-radius: var(--border-radius); margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <strong>Butterfly</strong>
    <p><span class="badge">Quarters</span></p>
  </a>
</div>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-catalog", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controls:</strong> a checkbox inside <code>.label</code> lays itself out as a row. In a row of filters its <code>1rem</code> bottom margin would push it off the centre line, so it is set to <code>0</code> here.</li>
    <li><strong>Surfaces:</strong> the filter form is a flat <code>.card-border</code> and each result a raised <code>.card</code>, so the results read as the things to pick up. The cover placeholder uses <code>--surface-strong</code>, the one step darker than the card; a real cover image goes in its place.</li>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> the count is <code>.text-secondary</code>, between the two surfaces, so it belongs to neither.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="events">
  <h2>Event list</h2>
  <p>
    Each event is a row: the date, what and where, and an add-to-calendar menu.
    The menu is a native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>, so it needs no script.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--padding)">
  <li class="card-border flex flip" style="align-items: center">
    <div style="text-align: center; min-width: 4rem">
      <small class="text-secondary">NOV</small>
      <div><strong style="font-size: 1.5rem">14</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1">
      <strong>Folding party</strong>
      <p class="text-secondary"><small>Saturday, 2 to 4 pm · Belmont Library</small></p>
    </div>
    <details style="position: relative">
      <summary class="btn btn-secondary">Add to calendar</summary>
      <ul class="dropdown-content menu" style="position: absolute; right: 0; margin-top: calc(var(--padding) / 4); list-style: none">
        <li><a href="#" class="semantic menu-item">Google Calendar</a></li>
        <li><a href="#" class="semantic menu-item">Apple / Outlook (.ics)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </li>
  <li class="card-border flex flip disabled" style="align-items: center">
    <div style="text-align: center; min-width: 4rem">
      <small class="text-secondary">OCT</small>
      <div><strong style="font-size: 1.5rem">03</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1">
      <strong>Zine swap</strong>
      <p class="text-secondary"><small>Past event · Community center</small></p>
    </div>
  </li>
</ul>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-events", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> the list is a grid for its gap, and each row is <code>.flex .flip</code>, so on a phone the date, details and button stack.</li>
    <li><strong>Surfaces:</strong> <code>.dropdown-content</code> only paints. Where it opens is the caller's job: a relative <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> and an absolute panel.</li>
    <li><strong>Boundary:</strong> a past event takes <code>.disabled</code>, which sets <code>--chroma: 0</code> on the row. Everything in it loses its colour together, with no per-element overrides.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Guide sections</h2>
  <p>
    Long how-to content folds into collapses, one per question. Each body is
    prose.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<details class="collapse" open>
  <summary class="collapse-title">How do I fold a quarter-page zine? <span>−</span></summary>
  <div class="collapse-content prose">
    <ol>
      <li>Fold the sheet in half along the long edge.</li>
      <li>Fold it in half again.</li>
      <li>Crease well and trim the top fold.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</details>
<details class="collapse">
  <summary class="collapse-title">Can I print double sided at home? <span>+</span></summary>
  <div class="collapse-content prose">
    <p>Yes. Flip on the short edge so the back pages are not upside down.</p>
  </div>
</details>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-faq", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Text:</strong> <code>.prose</code> goes on <code>.collapse-content</code>, not on the stack, so the titles keep their own size and spacing.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="cta">
  <h2>Credit band</h2>
  <p>
    A small block that belongs to someone else, in their colour, at the foot of
    the page.
  </p>
  {% set classless %}
<aside class="card-border retheme flex flip" style="--primary: rebeccapurple; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between">
  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Want a site like this?</h3>
    <p class="text-secondary">Built by a one-person studio in Portland.</p>
  </div>
  <a href="#" class="btn">Book a free call</a>
</aside>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-cta", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Boundary:</strong> <code>.retheme</code> with the studio's own <code>--primary</code> marks the block as separate from the group's theme without a single extra rule.</li>
    <li><strong>Spacing:</strong> the prose column keeps its bottom margins; <code>align-items: center</code> on the row centres the button against the whole block.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="footer">
  <h2>Footer with a disclaimer</h2>
  {% set classless %}
<footer>
  <hr class="divider" />
  <nav class="flex" style="flex-wrap: wrap; gap: calc(var(--padding) / 2) var(--padding)">
    <a href="#" class="link">Zine Catalog</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">How to Help</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Events</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Community Kit</a>
    <a href="#" class="link">Get in Touch</a>
  </nav>
  <p class="text-secondary" style="margin-top: var(--padding)">
    <small>This is a platform for independent voices. Zines are the responsibility of their creators and are not endorsed by this site.</small>
  </p>
</footer>
  {% endset %}
  {{ m.demo("community-footer", classless) }}
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> one wrapping <code>.flex</code> row with a smaller row gap than column gap, so wrapped links read as one list rather than as stacked rows.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endblock %}
